test: complete synthetic Linux man page with self-contained default Go fonts
-- input.1 --
.\" Synthetic fixture; no installed man database or resources required.
.TH MAN-TOOL 1 "2026-10-21" "Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
man-tool \- inspect a source document
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY man-tool
.OP \-v
.OP \-o file
.I input
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read
.I input
and inspect its structure.
.PP
Output preserves the original source independently of canonical text.
.SS "Input formats"
The first implementation handles typical Linux man pages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 8
.B \-v
Display verbose diagnostics
on standard error.
.TP
.BI "\-o " file
Write the selected document to
.IR file .
.IP \(bu 2
No automatic includes or external commands.
.RS 4
Indented explanatory text.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
  man-tool -v input.1
  man-tool -o output.txt input.1
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR man 7 ,
.MR printf 3
.SH AUTHORS
.UR https://example.invalid/man-tool
Example maintainers
.UE .
